          ],
          "evidence_strength": "Strong demand evidence (checklist burden, academic motivation, forum threads). Direct prior art exists, so novelty is the issue. Independent sources: kernel docs, Yocto list, Arch forum, KUnit docs. Adoption of klocalizer is not visible on LKML or forums (17, 168). Only the kismet part of the kmax suite is confirmed to be in 0-day (27, 197).",
          "existing_solutions": "klocalizer/krepair/koverage (kmax suite, FSE 2024); undertaker/Vampyr (stale, about Linux 3.2); merge_config.sh; localmodconfig; kernelconfig.io; menuconfig search.",
          "remaining_gap": "Gaps the claims state for klocalizer: no accuracy validation of its Kbuild constraints (it says the formulas may be inexact), composite-object and CONFIG_BROKEN handling, one architecture per invocation, heavy SuperC/Java setup, header-only patches unsupported, constraint collection 2-15 minutes (274). No explanation chain. Non-Linux Kbuild trees are not targeted. kfold must be benchmarked head-to-head on the same patches.",
          "kfold_fit": "object-selection",
          "kfold_fit_reason": "This is the core of config-for. The fit is real but not novel: klocalizer already solves the problem at finer (line) granularity. Differentiation must rest on speed, exactness of Kbuild semantics, explanations, and other Kbuild trees."
        },
        {
          "id": "P3",
          "name": "Stable and backport build breakage in specific arch/config pairs (H3)",
