          "description": "Bugs depending on preprocessor conditionals (Abal et al., Mordahl et al. report about 80% variability warnings from bug finders on sampled configs), dead #ifdef blocks (undertaker/Vampyr, 78.49% allyesconfig block coverage in 2.6.35), and the 2021 dead-code cleanup. Kbuild-level coding style pushes variability out of .c files, but '#ifdef use should be confined to header files' leaves them.",
          "who_has_it": "Kernel researchers, maintainers of dead code, static analysis users",
          "claim_indices": [
            3,
            14,
            15,
            83,
            87,
            88,
            95,
            96,
            97,
            230,
            250
          ],
          "evidence_strength": "Strong in the literature, but dated (2011-2019) and out of scope.",
          "existing_solutions": "undertaker/Vampyr (stale), SuperC-based klocalizer, checkkconfigsymbols.py, TypeChef, Coccinelle.",
          "remaining_gap": "File-internal conditions.",
          "kfold_fit": "out-of-scope",
          "kfold_fit_reason": "The C preprocessor is excluded from kfold. State it as a limitation (the krepair line-level numbers include #ifdef arms)."
        },
