          "name": "Existing tool: klocalizer/krepair/koverage (Kmax suite) already solves config-for and patch coverage",
          "description": "The most serious competitor. klocalizer produces a config including a compilation unit, repairs configs for a patch, handles #ifdef via SuperC, and emits multiple configs. koverage measures patch coverage and kismet is integrated in 0-day. Reported: 98.5% mean coverage on 507 patches, 18 build errors found, 97% of patches need one config. Limits stated: Kbuild constraint accuracy not validated, header-only patches (2%), one arch per run, heavy setup, up to 23 configs worst case, formulas possibly inexact. Kmax has been shown to find 17% more C files than heuristic parsers; KBuildMiner and GOLEM are older and slower or less reliable. Nguyen & Nguyen (ICSME 2020) is the closest approach in method (only the record was confirmed). No visible developer adoption on LKML or forums (17, 168).",
