      "citable_statistics": [
        "Defconfig covers 21.7% of patched lines on average, one randconfig 29.2%, allyesconfig 88.5%, krepair-repaired defconfig 98.5%; 507 patches sampled from about 71,000 in one year (FSE 2024 krepair). Line-level, includes #ifdef arms. [claims 53,77,111] https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.17966",
        "allyesconfig takes about 4 hours versus about 20 minutes for defconfig or a repaired config (10.5x), and still leaves about 11.5% of patched lines uncovered. [79,111,173] https://arxiv.org/html/2404.17966v1 (the OSS 2022 slides say 3 hours, so cite the paper)",
        "Of 36,115 Intel 0-day build reports carrying configs (Oct 2019 - Aug 2022): 63% randconfig, 15% allyesconfig, 7% defconfig and 7% allmodconfig. [53,78,174] https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.17966",
        "Linux v5.13 x86, 13,411 commits: defconfig fully covers 1,688 and one randconfig 2,189; 8,853 and 8,333 are not covered (1,296 non-x86 and 1,177 header-only excluded). [49] https://paulgazzillo.com/files/oss2022.pdf",
        "About 11% of patches need cross-compilation, about 2% touch only headers, and a single config suffices for 97% of patches. [175,82] https://arxiv.org/html/2404.17966v1",
        "Linux 6.16 has 32,468 Kconfig options on x86_64, the configuration count has 6,550 digits, and coverage by testing is unknown. [26] https://lwn.net/Articles/1034811/",
        "A 0-day BUILD SUCCESS report for a tip branch (Feb 2025) tested 19 configs and skipped 125, only i386 and x86_64; an Apr 2025 report: 19 tested, 140 skipped. [177,266] https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/2502.2/01971.html",
        "Linaro LKFT 2024: 271 LTS releases tested, about 430k builds, about 400 builds per trigger. [179] https://foss-north.se/2025/slides/aroxell-kerneltesting-slides.pdf",
        "KernelCI (Sept 2024): over 220 build configurations, boot tests on 45 hardware platforms. [62,183] https://kernelci.org/blog/2024/09/12/bring-your-tree-to-the-new-kernelci/",
        "Kernel CNA issues about 60 CVEs per week; Linux has about 85,000 files of which typically 5-10% are used; with the CIP defconfig 90-95% of 2024 CVEs were judged not relevant; at 4.19 EOL about 56% of about 1000 unfixed CVEs could be excluded. [154] https://opensource.siemens.com/events/2025/slides/Christoph_Steiger__Triaging_CVEs_for_the_Linux_Kernel.pdf",
        "Kmax found 9,044 C files in x86 Linux 2.6.33.3 where earlier heuristic studies counted at most 7,691 (about 17% more); 1,985 Makefiles controlling 19,651 C files in a later version. [115,116] https://paulgazzillo.com/papers/esecfse17.pdf",
        "kismet: 781 alarms (151 after sharing), 100% precision, 38 reports confirmed and 15 patches committed; randconfig found only 98 alarms in the same time. [94,120] https://doi.org/10.1145/3468264.3468578",
        "Kconfirm v4 (July 2026): 1,282 default-check alarms on x86-64 at v7.2-rc4. [165] https://lkml.iu.edu/2607.3/03886.html",
        "PatchLens (FSE 2026): CVE text names the needed configuration option for about 1% of cases (recall); average 1.84 variables per predicate on Linux. [123] https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.25863",
        "Hovold's Nov 2025 - Jan 2026 campaign enabled COMPILE_TEST for at least five drivers that no standard build covered (at_hdmac, bcm2835 dmaengine, tegra iommu, omap-ocp2scp, k3-socinfo). [0,1] https://lkml.iu.edu/2511.2/04659.html",
        "Allyesconfig selects only 78.49% of selectable #ifdef blocks on Linux 2.6.35 x86 (older, block-level, partly out of scope). [83] https://sigops.org/s/conferences/sosp/2011/workshops/plos/02-tartler.pdf",
        "Syzbot (LPC 2023): about 17k findings, patch-test requests rose from about 300 (2018) to about 1,000 per year (2021-22). [184,185] https://lpc.events/event/17/contributions/1521/attachments/1272/2698/LPC%2723_%20Syzbot_%207%20years%20of%20continuous%20kernel%20fuzzing.pdf",
        "A manual study of Linux 4.4.1 found 80 mismatches between Kconfig and the build system or code; about two-thirds may lead to misconfigurations. [101,294] https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.05828"
      ],
